      "code": "while (i < GF_ARRAY_LENGTH(str)) {",
      "note": "On the exact witness, step 5 leaves `p->size == 1042`, already larger than `GF_ARRAY_LENGTH(str) == 1024`. The patch fixes this obligation by replacing the fixed stack buffer with `gf_malloc(sizeof(char) * (p->size + 1))`, changing the loop bound to `while (i < msize)`, and rejecting the no-NUL case with `if (i == msize) return GF_ISOM_INVALID_FILE;`.",
